CPEDAL 1
NAME "Fuzz Factory Reference"

# Classic five-knob Fuzz Factory topology, cross-checked against the supplied
# Effects Layouts drawing and the Aion/verified public schematic.
#
# Q2/Q3 use separate compact AC128 gain bins (about 70 and 110 hFE) because
# matched low/high germanium devices are part of the characteristic topology.
# Power-protection and indicator-LED parts are omitted from the audio model.

V VCCSRC VCC 0 9
AUDIO GUITAR INPUT 0 0.20

# Optional input pulldown shown in several verified DIY implementations.
R R_IN_PD INPUT 0 1M
C C1 INPUT Q1B 10u

# Q1: 2N3904 input boost with collector-to-base feedback.
R R1 Q1C Q1B 220k
Q Q1 Q1C Q1B 0 2N3904

# STAB is wired as a rheostat in series with the supply. Increasing the GUI
# control corresponds to the normal clockwise/stable direction (less series R).
POT STAB VCC VCC STAB_RAIL 5k LIN 1.0
R R2 STAB_RAIL Q1C 10k

# Q2: lower-gain PNP germanium stage. The characteristic 47k feedback/bias
# resistor returns from Q2 base to the Q3-emitter / COMP-DRIVE node; it does
# not return directly to the STAB rail.
C C2 Q1C Q2B 100n
R R4 Q3E Q2B 47k
PNP Q2 Q2C Q2B STAB_RAIL AC128_LOW

# GATE varies Q2 collector loading. Physical lugs 1+2 are grounded, so a
# clockwise/high GUI setting reduces resistance after the fixed 470 ohms.
R R3 Q2C GATE_TOP 470
POT GATE 0 0 GATE_TOP 10k LIN 0.0

# Q3 base is driven directly from Q2 collector.
# COMP is the Q3 emitter feed from the STAB rail (physical lugs 1+2 tied).
POT COMP Q3E Q3E STAB_RAIL 10k LIN 0.2

# DRIVE is a 10k emitter-path pot with its wiper AC-bypassed back to the rail.
# At 100% the 10u capacitor bypasses the full pot for maximum fuzz gain.
POT DRIVE STAB_RAIL DRIVE_W Q3E 10k LIN 0.5
C C3 DRIVE_W STAB_RAIL 10u

PNP Q3 Q3C Q2C Q3E AC128_HIGH

# Output collector load and volume control.
R R5 Q3C VOL_TOP 5k1
POT VOLUME 0 VOL_W VOL_TOP 5k LIN 0.3
C C4 VOL_W OUT 10u
R R6 OUT 0 220k

OUTPUT OUT 1
